WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.796
Zones and conduits turn risk analysis into architectural boundaries.

00:00:04.796 --> 00:00:15.530
A zone groups logical or physical assets that share security requirements based on factors such as function, criticality, consequence, ownership, and exposure.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:23.067
A zone should represent a meaningful trust decision, not merely an existing subnet or room.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:27.863
A conduit is a controlled communication path between zones.

00:00:27.863 --> 00:00:35.856
It carries the data and services that the operation requires while enforcing the boundary's security expectations.

00:00:35.856 --> 00:00:42.479
Teams should document approved sources, destinations, protocols, direction, purpose, users, and administrative ownership.

00:00:42.479 --> 00:00:49.559
For example, an enterprise reporting system may need production data from a site historian.

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:54.812
That requirement does not justify direct enterprise access to controllers.

00:00:54.812 --> 00:01:03.719
An intermediary service in an industrial DMZ can replicate required data while reducing reachability toward lower-level control functions.

00:01:03.719 --> 00:01:08.971
Zone design should distinguish systems with different risk and capability.

00:01:08.971 --> 00:01:17.422
Safety functions, control areas, engineering services, remote access, wireless devices, and legacy equipment may warrant separate treatment.

00:01:17.422 --> 00:01:25.872
Conduits should also account for administration, updates, backups, authentication, and vendor support, not only routine production traffic.

00:01:25.872 --> 00:01:34.322
Segmentation technology implements part of the design, but a firewall alone does not create a defensible zone.

00:01:34.322 --> 00:01:41.402
The boundary needs current inventory, documented flows, secure configuration, monitoring, ownership, and change control.

00:01:41.402 --> 00:01:47.568
Teams must also test that restrictions preserve timing, redundancy, failover, and recovery.

00:01:47.568 --> 00:01:52.364
Review zones and conduits when architecture or risk changes.

00:01:52.364 --> 00:02:01.271
Cloud analytics, new vendors, temporary maintenance links, and production expansions can introduce paths that bypass the intended model.

00:02:01.271 --> 00:02:08.351
The objective is necessary, limited, observable communication between assets with clearly understood trust relationships.
